The only thing that prevents corpses from decaying (at least, for those
corpses that DO decay...a lizard corpse is safe forever) is an icebox.

An icebox is very...VERY heavy, and constantly throwing the cockatrice
corpse into it every time you wanted to walk around would be...impractical.

Dropping a corpse onto ice will prolong the decay timer, but not eliminate
it.

Honestly, for as powerful as a rubber chicken is, if there was a convenient
way to keep one around indefinitely, the game would just be ridiculously
too easy. As soon as you got a cockatrice corpse, the X method of
preserving it, and a pair of gloves, there would be only like 15 monster
species in the whole game that would pose any sort of threat to you...and 3
of them are the Riders.


